 "about": "Every model Hearth Forge can use (docs/mockups/hearth-forge/02-models.png, the owner's approved board of Nov 26, 2026). What each makes, the memory it needs and whether it fits 12 GB are each maker's own figures (Nov 2026); the licence is the maker's. Weights come only from each model's own Hugging Face repo, only when you press Get: every file is checked against the SHA-256 Hugging Face lists for it at the pinned revision (\"revision\"; empty means Hearth pins the commit Hugging Face names at your first Get and keeps to it, in ~/Hearth/Forge/models/forge-lock.json). \"runner\" is the model's own code Hearth Forge runs it with (runners below, each a pinned git commit); a model without one can be got and kept, and Hearth Forge says plainly it can't make with it yet. Built into the app (and its Store updates): one copy, read by the app and by hearth-forge on the Nvidia PC.",
